lane: producers-chunked-consumer
why: ManyProducersBenchmark -- written by me today -- compares our
  ELEMENTWISE consumer (receiveBlocking per element) against zio's
  CHUNKED one (ZStream.fromQueue.collectWhileSome.runForeach). Fifth
  appearance of the mismatch I spent the day correcting elsewhere, and
  this time I introduced it.
  It makes the one row where zio still leads that table (285.4 against
  350.4 at a single producer) unreadable, and understates every okay
  lane in it.
how: add a chunked consumer to every okay lane, keep the elementwise
  one as a DIAGNOSTIC row, and name every lane by its granularity as
  the rule now requires. Re-measure the sweep.
